This file will hold Keeper's public release-signing key (OpenPGP, ASCII-armoured).

It is a placeholder: no signing key has been published yet, so releases carry no .asc
signatures. Until then, verify downloads with SHA256SUMS.txt, the Sigstore (cosign)
signature of SHA256SUMS.txt and GitHub's build attestations; see docs/INSTALL.md.

For maintainers, once:
  1. On an offline or trusted machine, create the key (never commit the private part):
       gpg --quick-gen-key "Keeper Releases <contact@ashforde.org>" ed25519 sign 3y
  2. Replace this file with the public key:
       gpg --armor --export "Keeper Releases" > KEYS/keeper-release.asc
  3. Store the private key as the repository secret KEEPER_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY:
       gpg --armor --export-secret-keys "Keeper Releases" | gh secret set KEEPER_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY
     and, if it has a passphrase, KEEPER_GPG_PASSPHRASE.
  4. Publish the fingerprint in SECURITY.md and docs/INSTALL.md.
From the next release on, the workflow signs SHA256SUMS.txt and each AppImage, and builds
the signed apt and dnf repositories.
